Based on all 8 reference image views, the visual evidence overwhelmingly points to Sooty Mould. The test image consistently matches the characteristics of Sooty Mould, which is a dark, superficial fungal growth on the leaf surface. The other diseases (Anthracnose, Die Back, Powdery Mildew) present with distinctly different symptoms (lesions, shriveling, white powdery growth).

